## 📌 Project Overview

This project aims to build an end-to-end analytical system using real-world e-commerce behavioral data.

Instead of stopping at exploratory data analysis and charts, the project follows a structured workflow:

> **Raw Data → Data Quality → Transformation → Data Warehouse → SQL Analytics → Business Insights**

The implementation is being developed **entirely in Kaggle Notebooks**, using DuckDB for analytical SQL processing and Parquet for columnar storage.

### 🎯 What this project aims to demonstrate

| Area | What it demonstrates |
|---|---|
| Data Engineering | Data ingestion, transformation, validation and efficient processing |
| SQL Analytics | Aggregations, CTEs, window functions and analytical queries |
| Data Modeling | Grain, fact tables, dimensions, keys and star schema design |
| Business Analytics | Revenue, conversion, product and customer performance |
| Customer Analytics | RFM, cohorts, repeat purchasing and retention |
| Data Visualization | Analytical charts and reporting-ready datasets |
| Data Quality | Validation rules, reconciliation and documented assumptions |

> **Project status:** This repository is under active development. Planned features are not represented as completed or production-validated work.

---

## 📊 Dataset

<div align="center">

### eCommerce Behavior Data from Multi-Category Store

[![Open Dataset on Kaggle](https://img.shields.io/badge/OPEN%20DATASET-KAGGLE-20BEFF?style=for-the-badge&logo=kaggle&logoColor=white)](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/mkechinov/ecommerce-behavior-data-from-multi-category-store)

</div>

The dataset contains event-level records of online shopping behavior, including product views, cart activity and purchases.

### Dataset fields

| Column | Description | Analytical use |
|---|---|---|
| `event_time` | Event timestamp | Time-series and cohort analysis |
| `event_type` | Type of interaction | Funnel and behavior analysis |
| `product_id` | Product identifier | Product performance |
| `category_id` | Category identifier | Category analysis |
| `category_code` | Product category code | Category-level reporting |
| `brand` | Brand name | Brand performance |
| `price` | Recorded product price | Purchase-value analysis |
| `user_id` | User identifier | Customer analysis |
| `user_session` | Session identifier | Session behavior |

### Event lifecycle

```text
        PRODUCT DISCOVERY
               │
               ▼
           ┌───────┐
           │ VIEW  │
           └───┬───┘
               │
               ▼
           ┌───────┐
           │ CART  │
           └───┬───┘
               │
        ┌──────┴──────┐
        │             │
        ▼             ▼
   REMOVE FROM     PURCHASE
      CART
```

**Processing note:** The full dataset is large. The project will inspect the exact files available in Kaggle before choosing an ingestion strategy. DuckDB will be used to avoid loading the entire dataset into Pandas unnecessarily.

