## 🏗️ Data Architecture

The intended architecture separates raw input, standardized data, warehouse modeling and analytical outputs.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["Kaggle Dataset"] --> B["Data Inspection"]
    B --> C["Raw Event Data"]
    C --> D["Data Quality Checks"]
    D --> E["DuckDB Staging Layer"]
    E --> F["Standardization & Enrichment"]
    F --> G["Dimensional Warehouse"]
    G --> H["SQL Analytics"]
    H --> I["Analytical Data Marts"]
    I --> J["Visualizations"]
    I --> K["Power BI-Ready Outputs"]

    classDef source fill:#DCEBFF,stroke:#2563EB,color:#172554
    classDef process fill:#E0F2FE,stroke:#0284C7,color:#0C4A6E
    classDef warehouse fill:#DCFCE7,stroke:#16A34A,color:#14532D
    classDef output fill:#F3E8FF,stroke:#9333EA,color:#581C87

    class A,C source
    class B,D,E,F,H process
    class G warehouse
    class I,J,K output
```

### Architecture layers

| Layer | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| Source | Kaggle dataset files |
| Raw | Preserve and inspect source records |
| Staging | Standardize names, types and formats |
| Enrichment | Derive dates and analytical attributes |
| Warehouse | Build fact and dimension tables |
| Analytics | Calculate business metrics using SQL |
| Marts | Produce focused customer, product and KPI tables |
| Reporting | Visualizations and Power BI-ready outputs |

---

## 🧱 Data Modeling

The initial design uses a **star schema**, subject to validation against the source data.

### What is a star schema?

A star schema is a dimensional modeling design in which a central fact table connects to descriptive dimension tables.

- **Fact table:** Records business events and measurable values.
- **Dimension table:** Describes entities used to filter, group and interpret facts.
- **Grain:** Defines exactly what one row represents.
- **Surrogate key:** A warehouse-generated identifier used to identify a dimension record.

### Proposed model

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    DATE["DIM_DATE"]
    USER["DIM_USER"]
    PRODUCT["DIM_PRODUCT"]
    CATEGORY["DIM_CATEGORY"]

    FACT["FACT_EVENT<br/>One source event per row"]

    DATE --> FACT
    USER --> FACT
    PRODUCT --> FACT
    CATEGORY --> FACT

    classDef fact fill:#DBEAFE,stroke:#2563EB,color:#172554
    classDef dim fill:#DCFCE7,stroke:#16A34A,color:#14532D

    class FACT fact
    class DATE,USER,PRODUCT,CATEGORY dim
```

### Planned warehouse tables

| Table | Intended grain | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `fact_event` | One source event per row | Event-level analysis |
| `dim_date` | One row per calendar date | Calendar and time analysis |
| `dim_user` | One row per user identifier | User-level analysis |
| `dim_product` | One row per product identifier | Product-level analysis |
| `dim_category` | One row per category identifier | Category-level analysis |

The model will be revised if profiling reveals additional entities, changing attributes, or key-quality problems.

